From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Sep 2026 13:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ath9k: demote ar9003_eeprom constant-conversion to warning

This tree builds with clang -Werror; ar9003_eeprom.c intentionally
narrows regdomain dBm table constants from int to u8, which clang flags
as -Wconstant-conversion errors. Demote the diagnostic for this file
only (ath9k_hw is pulled in by CONFIG_ATH9K_HTC for the NetHunter
external-USB-WiFi phase).
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/Makefile | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/Makefile b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/Makefile
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/Makefile
@@ -74,3 +74,8 @@
 ath9k_htc-$(CONFIG_ATH9K_HTC_DEBUGFS) += htc_drv_debug.o
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_ATH9K_HTC) += ath9k_htc.o
+
+# 2026-09-14: clang -Werror turns the eeprom regdomain int->u8 narrowing
+# into a hard error on this 4.4 tree; the values are intentional (dBm
+# tables), so demote just this file.
+CFLAGS_ar9003_eeprom.o += -Wno-constant-conversion
-- 
2.39.0
